Expose the existing firmware scratch byte and optional PMCTRL_S5
power-reason byte as read-only diagnostics. Preserve the warning that
firmware scratch can be stale across an ordinary reset.

The public CIX material does not define the complete power-reason enum.
Mark the inherited interpretations with an assumed- prefix and keep
unmapped values unknown. CIX EDK2 reads the same register, masks its low
three bits, and treats 0x07 as the four-second power-button override, so
use that source-backed mapping instead of the previous CSU watchdog label.
Do not invent a replacement meaning for 0x06.

Keep the register reader deliberately narrow: both diagnostic registers
have the same byte-wide ABI, so a caller-supplied mask would imply a
variation that the hardware interface does not have.

diff --git a/Documentation/ABI/testing/sysfs-driver-sky1-reboot-reason b/Documentation/ABI/testing/sysfs-driver-sky1-reboot-reason
