@@ -0,0 +1,36 @@
+What:		/sys/bus/platform/devices/*/firmware_scratch_raw
+Date:		July 2026
+Contact:	Gentoo CIX kernel maintainers
+Description:
+		Read-only hexadecimal value from the low byte of the CIX Sky1
+		firmware scratch register described by the device's first memory
+		resource. Firmware may leave this value unchanged across an ordinary
+		reset, so it must not be treated as a guaranteed last-reset cause.
+
+What:		/sys/bus/platform/devices/*/firmware_scratch_reason
+Date:		July 2026
+Contact:	Gentoo CIX kernel maintainers
+Description:
+		Read-only diagnostic decoding of firmware_scratch_raw. Known values
+		are power-on-or-unknown, default-exception, watchdog-interrupt,
+		warm-reset and invalid; all other values are reported as unknown.
+
+What:		/sys/bus/platform/devices/*/hardware_reason_raw
+Date:		July 2026
+Contact:	Gentoo CIX kernel maintainers
+Description:
+		Read-only hexadecimal value from the optional CIX Sky1 hardware
+		reset-reason register described by the device's second memory
+		resource. The file is absent when firmware omits that resource.
+
+What:		/sys/bus/platform/devices/*/hardware_reason
+Date:		July 2026
+Contact:	Gentoo CIX kernel maintainers
+Description:
+		Read-only diagnostic decoding of hardware_reason_raw. The file is
+		absent when firmware omits the hardware-reason resource. Labels with
+		the assumed- prefix are provisional interpretations rather than a
+		stable hardware specification; hardware_reason_raw remains
+		authoritative. CIX firmware independently identifies low-three-bit
+		value 0x07 as the four-second power-button override. Value 0x06 and
+		all other unmapped values are reported as unknown.
